                            {
                                "target_word": "Jew",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3fa7117f-18b6-355b-8323-c434bfee8506",
                                        "entry_id": "334ee5c8-cd4a-3f99-968e-2f071a53f3a3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Jewish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "offensive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0b2dff4-4a9a-465e-91e3-88e0915fcddc",
                                                "sense_id": "3fa7117f-18b6-355b-8323-c434bfee8506",
                                                "text": "Whenever a Jew nose casts its sinister shadow over the register, the hotel-keeper suddenly discovers that his hostelry is full to overflowing, and profoundly, but firmly, regrets his inability to receive any more guests."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2399cf0-817b-4657-b149-150d01d93c60",
                                                "sense_id": "3fa7117f-18b6-355b-8323-c434bfee8506",
                                                "text": "\"Started that Jew country on top of everything else, and then all hell broke loose ever since.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Jew",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54faa712-03f5-3765-b4b7-dfbddc9ec98b",
                                        "entry_id": "8aa66ea5-9cb8-3e6e-96e3-0bff5473acf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make (more) Jewish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "offensive",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f331b20-4293-4ed5-95f4-b94210b3872d",
                                                "sense_id": "54faa712-03f5-3765-b4b7-dfbddc9ec98b",
                                                "text": "1991, E. Sicher, The Jewing of Skylock: Wesker's The Merchant” (MLS 21 (1991), 57–69)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2211001a-9cd6-4ae9-9d07-414fcfe15d77",
                                                "sense_id": "54faa712-03f5-3765-b4b7-dfbddc9ec98b",
                                                "text": "Portia's “Jewing” of Shylock has long been noticed by many critics. For an early example see, for example, the anonymous essay “shylock the Jew-ed,” Temple Bar 45 (1875): 65–70. 45. These words have potentially “commercial” etymologies,[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4f6a89e-1d2d-4034-a6e5-e04e64072a49",
                                                "sense_id": "54faa712-03f5-3765-b4b7-dfbddc9ec98b",
                                                "text": "In both cases, the Jews used Blacks as political\nweapons to wreck healthy White countries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f5a67e7-0fb7-4189-9e5b-62ab9c93154e",
                                                "sense_id": "54faa712-03f5-3765-b4b7-dfbddc9ec98b",
                                                "text": "Queering the Jew and Jewing the Queer [by] Ri J. Turner. Editor's Note: Interlaced with personal narrative, Ri Turner's essay contributes to an ongoing discussion within Jewish gender studies concerning the relationship between Jewishness and queerness and factors the term genderqueer into both sides of the equation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c9fa225e-681e-396a-afea-0fb719f5746b",
                                        "entry_id": "8aa66ea5-9cb8-3e6e-96e3-0bff5473acf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To haggle or swindle in order to obtain a better deal (from someone)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive",
                                            "offensive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d7cd213-7b19-41b9-b54a-b51657d9cf01",
                                                "sense_id": "c9fa225e-681e-396a-afea-0fb719f5746b",
                                                "text": "They stops you on the sly in the streets, and tells you to call at their house at sitch a hour of the day, and when you goes there they smuggles you quietly into some room by yourselves, and then sets to work Jewing away as hard as they can, prizing up their own things, and downcrying yourn."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab900232-c464-4823-8147-3970dc4c1bdf",
                                                "sense_id": "c9fa225e-681e-396a-afea-0fb719f5746b",
                                                "text": "I just feel like you are Jewing me out of my money. I never asked you to give me anything the entire time that you were not working. Your mom told me that you got a lot of money from the insurance that Warren gave you."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "014c64ba-0927-410f-85f1-eac8cc207a6e",
                                                "sense_id": "c9fa225e-681e-396a-afea-0fb719f5746b",
                                                "text": "Then that bastard Keith showed up and did something even worse than Jewing me out of my pay: he blew the living freaking crap out of the one and only stereotype I still had to hold on to. He thanked me for my hard work,[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "879a7990-4047-40ee-af91-4d375c62137a",
                                                "sense_id": "c9fa225e-681e-396a-afea-0fb719f5746b",
                                                "text": "In the neighborhood I grew up in, it was common for haggling over price to include the admonition “stop Jewing me!” Even as children, we would say this. It goes without saying that this was an insensitive term[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6066b4f6-f0ed-4512-b75d-bb8581c3d962",
